# US21 - As a tutor with several tutorings committed, I want to see together whom I teach, when and
# about what, so that I organise my week and arrive prepared to each session.
#
# Each scenario runs over HTTP against a real PostgreSQL, with the same name, in
# TutorAgendaAcceptanceTest, signed in with real session tokens (TS03). The tutor's hours are
# generated by declaring the availability over HTTP and the students book them over HTTP, as they
# do in US19 and US03. What the agenda shows is covered without Spring by TutorAgendaTest.
# GET /api/v1/tutor/agenda answers a period of days of the university's zone, and
# GET /api/v1/tutor/agenda/history what is already over.

Feature: The tutor's agenda

  Background:
    Given I am a tutor of my university free tomorrow from nine to twelve, Lima time

  Scenario: Sorted agenda
    Given I have confirmed tutorings
    When I open my agenda
    Then I see them from the nearest to the farthest with the course or skill, the student, the date, the time and the need they described

  Scenario: A tutoring about to start
    Given one of my tutorings starts in less than fifteen minutes
    When I see my agenda
    Then that one is highlighted as one I can enter now

  Scenario: Telling what is booked from what is free
    Given in the same week I have hours booked and hours still free
    When I see my agenda
    Then I can tell which ones are taken and which ones are still available

  Scenario: Consulting the tutorings already taught
    Given I already taught tutorings
    When I open my agenda
    Then I can consult the history apart from the upcoming ones

  # Not a scenario of the story: the days of the agenda are those of the university.
  Scenario: The agenda is read in the university's time zone
    Given an hour late in the evening in Lima, which is already the next day in UTC
    When I ask for the agenda of that day
    Then it is on that day, with its time in Lima
    And a period backwards or longer than a month is refused

  # Not built, for the same reason as in US04: the session's identifier is sessions', and booking
  # cannot ask sessions for it without the two modules depending on each other.
  @pending
  Scenario: The highlighted tutoring opens its session
    Given one of my tutorings starts in less than fifteen minutes
    When I choose it in my agenda
    Then I enter its session
